AppInfo |
    @HL-ALib Resource Compiler V. {}.{}
    (c) 2023-{} AWorx GmbH. Published under MIT License (Open Source).
    For more information, see: https://alib.dev/alib_mod_resources.html
    @HL-

MSNGRCFILE   No resource file name given.
MSNGCPPFILE  No C++ file name given.

NOTACCESSIBLE  File {!Q} is not accessible.
UKNFILE        Unknown error with file {!Q}.
ISDIR          Given path {!Q} is a directory instead of a file.

DryRunStart    ALibRC dry-run mode.
DryRunEnd      ALibRC dry-run done.

//-------------------- CLI Commands/Options/Parameters/ExitCodes --------------------
ARCO<       ALibRC::Options::
//enum  ident        minread    identChar   in-arg-separ.   args to consume    ShortcutTo
ARCO ~|
  1,    validate      ,1,          v,          =               ,0                ,


ARCE<  ALibRC::ExitCodes::
ARCE ~|
  101,ErrMissingRCFilename     ,
  102,ErrRCFileNotFound        ,
  103,ErrRCFileNotAccessible   ,
  104,ErrMissingCPPFilename    ,
  105,ErrCPPFileNotFound       ,
  106,ErrCPPFileNotAccessible  ,
  107,ErrInResources

TExit101   No input resource file name given.
TExit102   Given resource file not found.
TExit103   Resource file is not readable.
TExit104   No C++ source file to patch given.
TExit105   Given C++ resource file not found.
TExit106   C++ file is not writable.
TExit107   The resource file is erroneous.

//-------------------- Help Texts --------------------
HlpCLIAppName  ALibRC

HlpUsage       "alibrc resourcefile cppfile"

HlpGeneral >
  \nABOUT ALibRC\n
  @>>This is a tool provided by the C++ Framework ALib that compiles external resources and inserts
  a corresponding code snippet into a C++ source file.
  The resources are specified in a resource file, while the C++ source file must exist and
  contain special markers for the insertion position.\n
  All details are given in the documentation of the ALib C++ Framework at:\n
    https://alib.dev/
  \n\n@<<

THlpCmdSht_validate     Parses the given resource file and checks for errors.
THlpCmdLng_validate >   Parses the given resource file and reports any errors.
                        No C++ code is generated and the cpp-file (if given) is not modified.

TOptUsg_validate        --validate resourcefile [cppfile]
TOptHlp_validate >
  If this option is given (anywhere in the command line), the resource file is only parsed and no
  C++ code is generated. The cpp-file parameter is ignored and can be omitted.


TOptUsg_format   --format[=]\"placeholders\"
TOptHlp_format  >
    Sets the output format. The format specification is given with the documentation of the
    ALib method CalendarDateTime::Format, found here:\n
    https://alib.dev/classalib_1_1strings_1_1util_1_1CalendarDateTime.html

THlpParSht_rc-file The '*.alibrc' input file.
THlpParLng_rc-file  =>
  Denotes the input file, usually of extension '*.alibrc'. This is a mandatory parameter to give.


